/*
 * bounded-loop.compact — only the two Compact for forms the reference allows.
 *
 * Official grammar (not an invented API):
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/compact/reference/compact-reference
 *   "for (const x of expr) stmt" over Vector, tuple, or Bytes
 *   "for (const i of start .. end) stmt" where start and end are literal
 *   unsigned integers or generic natural-number parameters, and end >= start
 * Recursion is disallowed. Loops must be bounded by a constant or by the
 * size of an object of constant size, because circuits must be finite.
 *
 * Upstream: midnightntwrk/midnight-docs#1387 (circuit-limit questions; the
 * Compact reference is owned by mn-codeowners-compact). This file does not
 * edit those pages and does not fix the public indexer or node.
 *
 * Language pin: Compact ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23. Not compiled here.
 *
 * Built by @kshot9000 https://x.com/kshot9000
